  "caveats": [
    "This is a controlled reduced-model replication, not a full-resolution reproduction of the published DNS.",
    "No measured dye profile or dye-depth series is included; dye comparisons are between matched numerical cases.",
    "Wind and extra-loss coefficients were fitted to the 15\u201320 s wave interval; later wave observations are held out.",
    "Measured characteristic slope contains the full surface; plotted simulation slope contains parent modes only.",
    "A finite initial Gaussian dye layer of fixed physical width is used on every grid; no evolution clipping or mass renormalization.",
    "Two grid spacings provide a resolution sensitivity check, not a formal convergence demonstration.",
    "Gaussian current noise has the same seed and RMS on both grids, but its spatial realization changes with the grid; refinement differences also include this perturbation sensitivity.",
    "Prognostic parents retain nine free modes with linear intrinsic evolution; nonlinear parent wave-wave interactions are omitted.",
    "More than 5% of parent action on either retained-band boundary flags possible spectral truncation; inspect the boundary-action checks before interpreting dye differences.",
    "Cho remains one-way and does not directly transport the mean-model dye or deposit turbulence.",
    "A clean validity stop is partial scientific output, not completion of the target interval."
  ],
